  "literature_notes": "OCLN is a four-pass transmembrane protein (tetraspanin-like claudin superfamily member) with an intracellular N-terminus (1\u201366), two extracellular loops EL1 (88\u2013139) and EL2 (195\u2013243), and a large intracellular C-terminal tail (266\u2013522). Every ledger line was examined:\n\nL1/L2/L3 (Flag-OCLN, full-length): The Flag tag is placed at the N-terminus (before residue 1). The N-terminus (1\u201366) is INTRACELLULAR per the authoritative topology landmarks. This is an intracellular tag; it does not qualify as an extracellular surface site. Recorded in other_positions.\n\nL4/L5 (Venus-OCLN, full-length): Same as above \u2014 N-terminal Venus fusion on full-length OCLN. The N-terminus is intracellular. L5 confirms functional HCV entry, but the tag faces the cytoplasm. Recorded in other_positions.\n\nL6/L7 (F-\u0394Occ): Mouse occludin was cut with BsaA1 in EL2 and the fragment placed downstream of a secretory signal peptide in pFLAG-CMV-1. This creates a secreted, soluble ectodomain construct \u2014 not a full-length membrane-anchored protein. Disqualified per the rules (soluble ectodomain secreted as a separate protein).\n\nL8/L9 (BL-Ocln / Ocln-BL with Myc): Full-length occludin fused to biotin ligase, with Myc at the C-terminal end (residue 522). The C-terminus (266\u2013522) is INTRACELLULAR. Recorded in other_positions.\n\nL10/L11 (VSV-G tagged chimeras): These are chimeras of connexin 32 transmembrane domains fused to occludin tail fragments (266\u2013372 and 373\u2013522). They are not full-length OCLN constructs; the VSV-G tag is on the intracellular occludin tail. Disqualified (chimeric, not full-length OCLN; intracellular tag).\n\nL12 (His-tagged domain fragments): Domain fragments (1\u2013160, 161\u2013265, 266\u2013522, 107\u2013139) expressed in pcDNA3.1. These are not full-length membrane-anchored constructs. Disqualified.\n\nNo ledger line reports a tag insertion on the extracellular face (EL1 or EL2) of full-length, membrane-anchored OCLN. The deletion mutants \u0394EL1 (94\u2013128) and \u0394EL2 (200\u2013238) named in L1 are deletions, not insertions, and do not qualify.",
